Footnote: † [The German habit of beginning open vowels with the 'check' or Arabic hamza, which is very marked, and instantly characterises his nationality, is probably what is here alluded to, as occasioning a sensation of much greater pressure. This does not apply in the least to English speakers.—*Translator.*]
